WEBVTT

00:22.981 --> 00:24.858
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:33.260 --> 01:35.011
I don't recognize this road.

01:35.095 --> 01:36.555
This <i>is</i> the way.

01:36.638 --> 01:37.848
Are you sure?

01:40.267 --> 01:42.102
Pick up the pace! Get a move on!

01:42.185 --> 01:43.270
I think we're stuck.

01:43.353 --> 01:44.646
Don't push!

01:44.729 --> 01:46.273
-Hey!
-Watch out--

01:51.027 --> 01:54.114
This open space
is where we fought the Red Dragon!

01:56.491 --> 01:59.995
You made it all the way here
on your last expedition?

02:00.745 --> 02:01.621
Yeah.

02:01.705 --> 02:04.875
For a long time, this spot
was believed to be the deepest point.

02:04.958 --> 02:09.087
But recently, they found a door nearby
that seems to go even deeper.

02:09.588 --> 02:12.883
It's engraved with a design,
and they think it opens with magic.

02:12.966 --> 02:16.887
<i>We came to sketch the design
for the Lord of the Island, but…</i>

02:19.931 --> 02:23.435
<i>You encountered the Red Dragon
and were forced to retreat.</i>

02:24.686 --> 02:26.730
All right, let's try our luck.

02:26.813 --> 02:29.107
I think we were over there last time.

02:31.151 --> 02:33.111
I found our gear!

02:33.695 --> 02:34.905
It's been ransacked.

02:34.988 --> 02:36.114
No!

02:38.200 --> 02:39.367
Yes!

02:39.451 --> 02:41.036
I found my sleeping bag!

02:41.119 --> 02:43.496
Great. My underwear's still here too.

02:43.580 --> 02:46.082
Those are things you prioritize
over your valuables?

02:47.083 --> 02:49.252
All our food is gone,

02:49.336 --> 02:51.338
but everything else seems untouched.

02:51.421 --> 02:53.214
Guess it was monsters that did this.

02:53.298 --> 02:54.591
I'm so glad.

02:54.674 --> 02:56.718
Now I can sleep warm tonight--

03:00.430 --> 03:01.806
That's not good.

03:01.890 --> 03:04.100
Let's find a place to rest for a bit.

03:04.184 --> 03:05.602
I want to organize my gear too.

03:06.102 --> 03:09.147
Maybe the snow slows down the Cleaners.

03:09.230 --> 03:11.274
They've gotten at my soap.

03:11.358 --> 03:12.317
Hey, none of that.

03:12.400 --> 03:14.444
Show me whatever you just stashed away.

03:17.822 --> 03:19.199
Here, Marcille.

03:19.282 --> 03:20.283
Ow.

03:20.367 --> 03:23.119
Talk about an untrained beast-man.

03:23.203 --> 03:25.789
No wonder they slapped that collar on you.

03:26.957 --> 03:29.209
You're called a half-foot, right?

03:29.292 --> 03:32.003
I've never seen your kind in the East.

03:32.087 --> 03:34.130
I had to come here
to learn about you folks.

03:35.257 --> 03:37.175
That odd name for your race.

03:37.259 --> 03:42.055
I heard it's because lots of you
got a foot lopped off for stealing.

03:43.556 --> 03:46.059
Come on, you two, cut it out.

03:47.060 --> 03:48.061
Marcille!

03:48.144 --> 03:49.312
Come here!

03:52.148 --> 03:53.984
It's a fish!

03:54.067 --> 03:57.570
Is there a way to cut out
just this section?

03:58.571 --> 04:00.824
Maybe with a magic circle…

04:01.449 --> 04:03.868
Right. Want to give it a shot, Laios?

04:03.952 --> 04:05.912
I'll show you how to draw a magic circle.

04:06.913 --> 04:08.790
How's your mana sickness been lately?

04:08.873 --> 04:10.625
I don't get so dizzy anymore.

04:11.543 --> 04:14.296
<i>The hallucinations
are getting stronger, though.</i>

04:15.297 --> 04:17.716
<i>It's fish I used to catch
on the fourth floor.</i>

04:19.342 --> 04:23.221
<i>The water from the upper floors
has flowed down here and froze.</i>

04:23.805 --> 04:26.975
<i>Looks like all sorts of stuff
end up in the stream.</i>

04:28.893 --> 04:30.478
And now the circle's ready.

04:31.062 --> 04:32.314
How do you feel?

04:32.397 --> 04:33.982
A little tired.

04:34.065 --> 04:36.109
I'll activate it then.

04:36.192 --> 04:40.530
Imagine it as pouring water
into the symbols you've etched.

04:44.367 --> 04:45.368
What on earth?

04:45.452 --> 04:46.995
The ground, it's…

04:50.582 --> 04:52.250
A-A monster?

04:52.334 --> 04:53.877
An Ice Golem?

04:58.006 --> 04:59.382
<i>I see.</i>

05:06.222 --> 05:07.140
Hey! Above you!

05:07.223 --> 05:08.141
Watch out!

05:11.102 --> 05:12.479
Laios!

05:24.449 --> 05:26.951
So how do we take this thing down?

05:27.035 --> 05:29.621
The only way to stop Golems
is by breaking their core!

05:29.704 --> 05:30.747
Their core?

05:30.830 --> 05:31.873
And where do I find that?

05:40.298 --> 05:41.883
Hey! Where's the core?

05:41.966 --> 05:43.551
Hang on a second!

05:43.635 --> 05:45.845
<i>Is that its core? No, it's just a fish.</i>

05:45.929 --> 05:47.972
<i>There's too much junk in there to tell.</i>

05:48.056 --> 05:51.101
Hey! Keep that thing distracted
and buy me some time!

05:51.184 --> 05:52.352
I can't spot the core yet!

05:52.435 --> 05:53.478
Huh?!

05:53.561 --> 05:58.358
<i>That jerk better not be making stuff up
to bring me down.</i>

06:05.240 --> 06:06.157
The snow!

06:16.918 --> 06:18.294
<i>It stopped.</i>

06:30.390 --> 06:31.516
Hey, you done yet?

06:31.599 --> 06:33.226
How much longer do I have to keep this up?

06:33.309 --> 06:34.978
That's good, Izutsumi. Well done!

06:41.568 --> 06:43.111
Good. Perfect!

06:44.237 --> 06:45.864
You better not be messing around!

06:45.947 --> 06:48.366
No, idiot. Check where my arrow landed.

06:52.453 --> 06:55.498
Also, I can use projectiles,

06:55.582 --> 06:58.459
but I can't do much damage with them.

06:58.543 --> 07:01.004
So don't count on me in a battle!

07:01.087 --> 07:02.338
I'll let you handle the rest!

07:05.758 --> 07:07.051
<i>Oh, well.</i>

07:07.135 --> 07:09.429
<i>Now that I know how to take it down…</i>

07:33.661 --> 07:38.208
Seems like I'm the only one here
who's actually useful.

07:38.291 --> 07:40.543
The rest of you are just…

07:48.134 --> 07:49.761
Is everyone okay?

07:49.844 --> 07:51.679
It'll warm up soon.

07:52.263 --> 07:55.475
That magic circle can get pretty hot,
so watch out for burns.

07:55.975 --> 07:58.394
Take off your wet clothes
and dry them out.

07:58.478 --> 07:59.437
You too.

07:59.521 --> 08:01.689
I'll give you some cover.

08:02.357 --> 08:04.025
Laios, can you change on your own?

08:06.027 --> 08:07.529
Someone lend him a hand.

08:09.197 --> 08:11.449
No need to shield me.

08:11.533 --> 08:13.451
But you can't just…

08:22.544 --> 08:26.005
It's not like anyone would be excited
to see a beast get naked.

08:27.006 --> 08:27.840
What's the big idea?

08:27.924 --> 08:30.635
I just didn't want you catching a chill.

08:30.718 --> 08:33.846
At least let me count her nipples,
or see the base of her tail!

08:38.851 --> 08:40.937
It's starting to get warm.

08:41.020 --> 08:43.648
Let's prepare something hot.

08:44.148 --> 08:46.568
We've got to thaw this out.

08:47.151 --> 08:49.696
Maybe I can melt it over the magic circle.

08:52.407 --> 08:53.950
Too close.

08:54.659 --> 08:55.952
This is nice, though.

08:56.035 --> 08:57.078
It feels like a sauna.

08:57.787 --> 08:59.831
It's been ages since we had a bath.

08:59.914 --> 09:01.416
Let's sweat it out!

09:07.255 --> 09:08.214
That thing comes off?

09:08.298 --> 09:09.591
Why am I blindfolded?

09:10.258 --> 09:13.469
<i>I'll clean the fish, then use the head
and bones to brew up some broth.</i>

09:14.053 --> 09:15.972
We might end up smelling like fish.

09:16.598 --> 09:19.475
<i>Thinly slice the mushrooms and Nightmares.</i>

09:19.559 --> 09:23.229
<i>Give the Shapeshifter meat a quick boil
to skim off any scum.</i>

09:23.896 --> 09:25.565
<i>Whisk the Harpy egg,</i>

09:25.648 --> 09:28.818
<i>then mix it in with the broth
and other ingredients.</i>

09:32.071 --> 09:33.990
<i>Pour it all into cups,</i>

09:34.073 --> 09:37.243
<i>set them in a pot
with the Ice Golem fragments,</i>

09:37.327 --> 09:38.286
<i>and heat it up.</i>

09:38.828 --> 09:41.247
Look. I made this out of her shed hair.

09:41.331 --> 09:42.248
How bored are you?

09:42.332 --> 09:45.627
Finally, garnish with Mandrake leaves.

09:45.710 --> 09:46.919
And it's done--

09:47.462 --> 09:48.421
Hey!

09:48.504 --> 09:50.840
You can't just start eating on your own.

09:50.923 --> 09:53.426
Wait until everyone is at the table.

09:53.509 --> 09:54.594
Why not?

09:54.677 --> 09:57.138
I took down the enemy all by myself!

09:57.221 --> 09:59.682
I deserve to eat first!

09:59.766 --> 10:02.685
Meals begin when everyone's present.

10:03.269 --> 10:06.272
Chilchuck, Laios went outside.
Can you go fetch him?

10:06.356 --> 10:07.190
Got it.

10:08.358 --> 10:10.193
This feels great.

10:10.276 --> 10:11.694
Is this guy for real?

10:11.778 --> 10:13.863
ICE GOLEM SAVORY EGG CUSTARD

10:13.946 --> 10:15.698
AND COOKED FISH
TAKEN FROM THE ICE GOLEM

10:16.282 --> 10:18.951
All right, now that we're all here,

10:19.035 --> 10:20.662
let's start eating!

10:20.745 --> 10:21.954
-Let's dig in.
-Let's dig in.

10:23.498 --> 10:24.457
It's pudding.

10:25.416 --> 10:27.126
Sorry, Marcille.

10:27.210 --> 10:28.336
Yum!

10:29.420 --> 10:30.672
<i>What a waste of time.</i>

10:30.755 --> 10:31.839
Hey, Izutsumi.

10:31.923 --> 10:33.508
What is it?

10:33.591 --> 10:34.717
This is for you.

10:35.301 --> 10:37.428
I patched up a torn bag.

10:37.512 --> 10:38.554
You can use it.

10:41.641 --> 10:42.475
Listen.

10:43.059 --> 10:45.019
I apologize for calling you a beast.

10:45.728 --> 10:47.313
I've got a sharp tongue.

10:47.814 --> 10:50.525
Traveling together
with a bunch of strangers

10:50.608 --> 10:53.152
can feel suffocating
and annoying at first.

10:53.653 --> 10:55.697
But once you get used to it,
there are perks.

10:56.322 --> 10:58.866
You can get others
to handle stuff you can't.

11:07.583 --> 11:09.419
-That was delicious.
-That was delicious.

11:10.711 --> 11:11.546
Yeah.

11:14.424 --> 11:15.883
Hey, are you done yet?

11:16.509 --> 11:17.844
Just a little longer.

11:18.344 --> 11:20.263
Like this and that…

11:20.346 --> 11:21.514
There we go!

11:22.765 --> 11:24.183
Ta-da!

11:26.352 --> 11:28.938
These are Namari's clothes,
but don't they suit her perfectly?

11:29.021 --> 11:30.440
They're hard to move in.

11:30.523 --> 11:32.817
It took some time to adjust them.

11:32.900 --> 11:34.360
I got all chilled again.

11:34.444 --> 11:35.736
I'm sorry, okay?

11:35.820 --> 11:36.863
Well, let's hit the road.

11:36.946 --> 11:37.780
Wait.

11:40.700 --> 11:43.411
These are Mandrakes boiled sweet.

11:43.494 --> 11:46.414
I figured they'd make
for good travel food.

11:50.460 --> 11:51.294
Hey.

11:52.503 --> 11:53.421
Have it.

11:55.006 --> 11:56.257
That's yours.

11:57.300 --> 11:58.176
I don't want it.

11:58.259 --> 11:59.302
Why not?

11:59.385 --> 12:00.887
It's really tasty.

12:00.970 --> 12:02.305
I said I don't want it.

12:02.388 --> 12:04.432
No, have a bite at least.

12:05.016 --> 12:06.309
-Try it!
-I said no!

12:09.145 --> 12:10.855
H-How mean!

12:10.938 --> 12:13.316
Why did she have
to draw blood in this situation?

12:14.275 --> 12:16.652
Just leave her be.
She'll eat when she's hungry.

12:17.737 --> 12:19.322
Why don't you want it?

12:19.405 --> 12:20.865
Because it's a monster.

12:20.948 --> 12:24.076
Everyone says that, but how is it
different from eating animals?

12:24.160 --> 12:27.747
If you eat monsters, you catch
strange diseases and turn into one!

12:27.830 --> 12:28.831
That's why I won't eat it!

12:29.415 --> 12:32.752
If eating monsters turned you into them,
it would be a simple story.

12:33.252 --> 12:35.630
It's the idea of becoming impure.

12:35.713 --> 12:37.798
It's not exactly logical,

12:37.882 --> 12:41.219
but I think most people, myself included,
avoid them for that reason.

12:41.802 --> 12:44.472
It feels like you're absorbing
something bad in some way.

12:44.555 --> 12:48.851
And with new diseases popping up
from creatures close to humans,

12:48.935 --> 12:52.480
I don't think vague aversion
should be brushed off so lightly.

12:55.316 --> 12:56.817
This is really good!

12:57.818 --> 13:02.740
But what did you do before
when you were served food you didn't like?

13:03.783 --> 13:04.825
Before?

13:07.328 --> 13:08.371
Ugh!

13:11.624 --> 13:13.000
Tade, you can have this.

13:14.335 --> 13:16.754
Thanks, Izu… I mean, Asebi!

13:17.338 --> 13:18.464
It never happened.

13:18.548 --> 13:19.632
I don't believe you.

13:19.715 --> 13:21.259
Let's go, you two!

13:32.019 --> 13:34.772
The blizzard doesn't seem to be easing up.

13:34.855 --> 13:37.567
Maybe we should just camp here for today.

13:37.650 --> 13:38.901
I'm hungry too.

13:39.569 --> 13:41.696
Senshi looks worn out as well.

13:41.779 --> 13:43.781
Let's whip something up ourselves.

13:43.864 --> 13:46.158
What ingredients do we have left?

13:46.242 --> 13:48.202
Nightmares, Mandrakes,

13:48.286 --> 13:49.620
eggs, mushrooms, and…

13:49.704 --> 13:50.538
What's this?

13:50.621 --> 13:52.081
Any fish?

13:52.164 --> 13:53.583
No, no more fish.

13:53.666 --> 13:54.750
Rice then.

13:54.834 --> 13:57.295
We're running low on rice too.

13:57.378 --> 13:59.964
Don't you have anything better than this?

14:00.047 --> 14:01.173
This is all we've got.

14:01.257 --> 14:03.050
Liar! You're hiding stuff!

14:03.134 --> 14:06.012
You can't afford to be
a picky eater in the dungeon.

14:06.095 --> 14:07.680
You should get used to it quickly.

14:07.763 --> 14:08.598
No!

14:08.681 --> 14:10.433
I only eat what I want to eat!

14:10.516 --> 14:12.101
Listen, Izutsumi.

14:12.184 --> 14:14.437
Eating monsters doesn't turn you into one.

14:15.021 --> 14:18.566
<i>Has anyone turned into a sheep
or pig after eating them?</i>

14:18.649 --> 14:22.028
<i>If a blind person eats an eyeball,
does that mean they'll see again?</i>

14:22.612 --> 14:25.448
<i>Sheep only eat grass,
but do they turn into plants?</i>

14:26.032 --> 14:29.368
Food and nutrition
are more complex than that.

14:29.452 --> 14:31.704
That's why people work hard to experiment.

14:31.787 --> 14:32.955
Shut up!

14:33.623 --> 14:35.291
What do you call that then?

14:35.374 --> 14:36.208
That?

14:40.838 --> 14:42.673
A sheep is growing into a tree.

14:43.257 --> 14:44.592
It's a Barometz.

14:44.675 --> 14:47.261
Why did it have to show up now?

14:47.345 --> 14:48.763
Listen, Izutsumi.

14:48.846 --> 14:50.264
That's a plant that always--

14:50.348 --> 14:52.767
Shut up! I'm sick of your talk!

14:52.850 --> 14:53.893
That's it.

14:53.976 --> 14:55.770
I'm going to get that sheep.

14:55.853 --> 14:57.146
What's a Barometz?

14:57.229 --> 14:58.606
Is it some kind of monster?

14:58.689 --> 15:01.025
It's a monster all right,
but it's harmless.

15:01.108 --> 15:02.026
Although,

15:02.109 --> 15:04.987
they do tend to attract carnivores.

15:05.988 --> 15:07.698
Be careful, Izutsumi.

15:07.782 --> 15:09.158
<i>Who does he think he's talking to?</i>

15:12.244 --> 15:13.537
It's not safe to stay here.

15:13.621 --> 15:15.665
-Let's harvest it quickly and--
-They're here.

15:15.748 --> 15:16.666
Huh?

15:20.586 --> 15:22.505
Dammit. Dire Wolves!

15:27.885 --> 15:29.929
M-My staff!

15:34.976 --> 15:36.060
Hold up!

15:36.143 --> 15:37.561
Where are you going?

15:37.645 --> 15:39.146
I hate dogs.

15:39.230 --> 15:41.023
They're smelly, noisy, and persistent.

15:41.649 --> 15:44.527
I-Is that reason enough
to just go off on your own?

15:45.319 --> 15:46.737
I left you guys to deal with them.

15:46.821 --> 15:50.992
You guys said friends are supposed
to make up for each other.

15:51.784 --> 15:54.078
That's not quite what we meant.

15:54.161 --> 15:55.371
Then what did you mean?

15:55.454 --> 15:58.332
You didn't join in on the fight
with the Golem back there.

15:58.416 --> 16:00.918
It's true we left that to you,

16:01.002 --> 16:02.837
but not because of personal preferences.

16:03.546 --> 16:05.840
Hey, let's turn back.

16:05.923 --> 16:07.091
No.

16:07.925 --> 16:10.261
<i>I'm catching a whiff of fire in the wind.</i>

16:10.344 --> 16:12.346
<i>If I follow it, I can find my way back.</i>

16:14.181 --> 16:15.099
Wait!

16:17.059 --> 16:19.228
<i>The scent's stronger to the right,</i>

16:19.311 --> 16:21.731
<i>but the path looks rough,
so I'll go this way.</i>

16:21.814 --> 16:23.983
Where are you heading?
Is this the right way?

16:24.567 --> 16:26.652
I'll take the path I want.

16:26.736 --> 16:28.612
You should do the same.

16:28.696 --> 16:31.240
Why don't you do as you like more?

16:31.323 --> 16:32.950
You hate eating monsters,

16:33.034 --> 16:35.244
and yet you still do it.

16:35.828 --> 16:37.163
It doesn't make sense.

16:37.872 --> 16:38.748
Well…

16:40.583 --> 16:42.877
It seems the wolves have come after us.

16:42.960 --> 16:44.128
Should we fight them here?

16:44.211 --> 16:46.589
I can use explosive spells,

16:46.672 --> 16:48.549
but I don't have my staff with me.

16:48.632 --> 16:50.676
And it's risky to cast them
in such a confined space.

16:50.760 --> 16:52.887
Maybe I can stun them with a bright light.

16:52.970 --> 16:54.555
I'll run and shake them off.

16:57.850 --> 17:00.269
What?!

17:15.117 --> 17:16.410
Ow!

17:18.621 --> 17:19.622
Owie.

17:20.623 --> 17:21.665
Ow.

17:23.626 --> 17:25.252
Hey, Asebi!

17:26.504 --> 17:29.924
You made Tade clear off the snow
from the roof of the training hall.

17:30.007 --> 17:30.925
I didn't.

17:31.008 --> 17:32.384
Don't lie to me!

17:32.468 --> 17:34.678
She fell from the roof while doing it.

17:34.762 --> 17:37.264
Unlike you, she's clumsy,

17:37.348 --> 17:39.809
so don't push tasks you dislike onto her!

17:39.892 --> 17:42.144
You should show more gratitude to us
for taking you in.

17:46.148 --> 17:47.274
Hey, Tade.

17:48.025 --> 17:50.569
Why did you go and do something
I never asked you to do?

17:50.653 --> 17:51.695
You really are dumb.

17:52.905 --> 17:54.615
But Tade…

17:56.117 --> 17:59.370
<i>What was it she said that day?</i>

18:00.162 --> 18:01.330
Never mind.

18:06.752 --> 18:07.753
<i>I slipped up.</i>

18:08.420 --> 18:10.297
<i>The explosion shifted
the wind's direction,</i>

18:10.381 --> 18:11.757
<i>and I failed to notice.</i>

18:17.513 --> 18:18.722
Close… your eyes.

18:19.598 --> 18:22.434
Close your eyes.

18:22.518 --> 18:24.812
Close them!

18:32.111 --> 18:34.029
T-Too close!

18:42.955 --> 18:43.789
Izutsumi!

18:44.832 --> 18:45.791
Are you alive?

18:46.667 --> 18:47.835
Ow!

18:47.918 --> 18:49.211
Your arm is broken.

18:49.295 --> 18:50.379
Can you walk?

18:50.462 --> 18:51.881
Let's rejoin the others.

18:59.180 --> 19:00.055
Listen.

19:00.639 --> 19:03.809
You asked me why I eat monsters,

19:04.435 --> 19:06.395
and I've been thinking about it.

19:06.478 --> 19:09.064
I have my goals and objectives.

19:09.148 --> 19:10.733
I want to help my friend

19:10.816 --> 19:13.068
and learn more about magic.

19:13.903 --> 19:17.114
So, I'm pushing toward those goals.

19:17.198 --> 19:19.533
Along the way,
I encounter things I dislike.

19:20.034 --> 19:22.536
Things that are bothersome,
things that tire me,

19:22.620 --> 19:24.788
and having to eat things I'd rather not.

19:25.789 --> 19:28.125
Individually, none of it is a big deal.

19:28.209 --> 19:31.795
But if I avoid everything I dislike,

19:31.879 --> 19:34.131
I'll stray further and further
from my path.

19:35.049 --> 19:37.259
Just like what's happening to us now.

19:38.928 --> 19:41.889
Why did you choose
to come along with us, Izutsumi?

19:42.431 --> 19:45.851
Because you said that
if we met the lunatic magician,

19:45.935 --> 19:48.437
there might be a chance
to break the curse on me.

19:48.520 --> 19:49.396
It's this way!

19:50.022 --> 19:51.065
Exactly.

19:51.148 --> 19:54.109
That's why you need to be ready
to take a few shortcuts.

20:00.991 --> 20:02.743
Izutsumi! Marcille!

20:02.826 --> 20:03.869
Are you okay?

20:03.953 --> 20:06.080
What about you guys?

20:06.163 --> 20:08.374
We were in a bit of a fix,

20:09.541 --> 20:11.961
<i>but Laios managed to scare them off,
so we're safe.</i>

20:12.044 --> 20:15.130
<i>Most of the wolves
went after Marcille, anyway.</i>

20:15.923 --> 20:17.091
Are you hurt?

20:17.174 --> 20:18.801
It seems she broke her arm.

20:19.301 --> 20:20.678
I'll use recovery magic on her

20:20.761 --> 20:22.805
while I set it back into place,
so lend me a hand.

20:28.727 --> 20:30.896
You did great.

20:30.980 --> 20:33.399
The recovery magic hurt more.

20:33.482 --> 20:36.068
I was hoping to harvest a Barometz,

20:36.151 --> 20:39.113
but the wolves made off
with the mature one.

20:39.196 --> 20:42.283
All that was left was this unripe fruit.

20:43.534 --> 20:44.994
Let's try cooking it.

20:53.127 --> 20:55.212
There's a sheep inside the fruit.

20:55.296 --> 20:56.380
I can't eat that!

20:56.463 --> 20:59.133
It's not the same as the others,
ethically speaking. I can't eat that!

20:59.216 --> 21:00.050
Yuck.

21:00.134 --> 21:03.804
Slice the Barometz ribs
into appropriate sizes,

21:03.887 --> 21:06.307
season them, and cook them.

21:06.390 --> 21:09.560
When both sides are nicely browned,

21:09.643 --> 21:12.938
pour in some wine,
cover with a lid, and let them steam.

21:13.022 --> 21:16.859
Run the rind of the fruit
through hot water, remove the peel,

21:16.942 --> 21:18.444
then chop it into chunks.

21:18.527 --> 21:21.196
Add garlic and stew together.

21:21.780 --> 21:24.950
Pour the finished sauce over the meat,

21:25.534 --> 21:26.452
and it's done.

21:26.535 --> 21:28.954
BAROMETZ BALUT (OR BAROMETZ CHOPS)

21:29.538 --> 21:30.956
Here, cat girl.

21:31.040 --> 21:32.291
This is yours.

21:33.042 --> 21:35.002
It's got weird stuff in it.

21:35.085 --> 21:38.297
That's the Barometz skin and shoots.

21:39.923 --> 21:42.343
You should've grilled the meat on its own.

21:49.933 --> 21:52.978
Barometz might look just like sheep,

21:53.062 --> 21:54.855
but they taste like crab!

21:54.938 --> 21:56.065
<i>So what?</i>

21:57.191 --> 21:58.233
<i>It's delicious.</i>

21:58.317 --> 22:00.861
<i>I never knew food this amazing existed.</i>

22:02.071 --> 22:03.364
<i>Come to think of it…</i>

22:03.989 --> 22:07.743
Tade, why did you go and do something
I never asked you to do?

22:08.410 --> 22:09.661
You really are dumb.

22:10.204 --> 22:11.705
Tade just wants

22:12.247 --> 22:15.042
to be helpful to everyone.

22:15.125 --> 22:16.126
Ow!

22:16.210 --> 22:18.420
I mean, this place is pretty great.

22:18.504 --> 22:22.382
We get three meals,
warm bedding, and baths too.

22:22.466 --> 22:24.927
I can't risk being kicked out.

22:25.010 --> 22:27.638
I'll do chores and anything else
to show them I'm useful!

22:29.848 --> 22:30.724
Asebi,

22:31.725 --> 22:34.895
don't lose your way just because
something is a bit bothersome.

22:37.481 --> 22:41.568
And Lady Maizuru sometimes
rewards me with snacks.

22:41.652 --> 22:43.737
That's what you're truly after, isn't it?

22:44.988 --> 22:46.365
<i>Maybe she's right.</i>

22:46.448 --> 22:49.701
<i>Sometimes you do end up
with something tasty out of it.</i>

22:53.247 --> 22:55.707
Good for you, Izutsumi!

22:55.791 --> 22:58.168
-Well done! Good girl!
-Good girl.

22:58.252 --> 23:00.129
Cut it out… You…

23:00.212 --> 23:03.757
What do you take me for, huh?!

23:04.258 --> 23:06.844
I'll only eat when I have no other choice.

23:06.927 --> 23:09.638
I won't be eating any vegetables
or monsters that taste bad, got it?

23:10.222 --> 23:13.142
But you won't know if they taste bad
until you give them a try.

23:13.225 --> 23:16.270
By the way, Marcille,
I noticed you're barely eating.

23:16.353 --> 23:18.689
Do you really think
you can get away with not eating

23:18.772 --> 23:20.649
after giving me that lecture?

23:21.817 --> 23:26.113
<i>Marcille deeply regretted
blocking her own means of escape.</i>

23:27.156 --> 23:28.532
<i>Dungeon food.</i>

23:28.615 --> 23:31.034
<i>Oh, dungeon food.</i>

25:00.165 --> 25:02.000
Subtitle translation by: Ai Matsuoka
